  "notes": [
    "Glyph loading, hinting and rasterization for the font backend (Docs/Design/Font/08-ThirdParty.ko.md section 8.2). The only Rocks consumer is the ClientOnly module TextLayoutBackend; HarfBuzz (hb-ft) and msdfgen (import-font) use it as well.",
    "Configuration is the documented FreeType way: include/freetype/config/ftoption.h and ftmodule.h are edited (traceable modifications, Rocks.patch). Consumers see the same configuration through the same headers, so no configuration define is passed around.",
    "zlib, Brotli and libpng are the Core Zlib, Core Brotli and LibPng modules. FT_CONFIG_OPTION_SYSTEM_ZLIB makes ftgzip.c include <zlib.h> instead of the bundled copy, which is not imported; ftgzip.c sets zalloc and zfree from FT_Memory, so the Z_SOLO zlib without a default allocator works.",
    "Allocation: the font backend creates the library with FT_New_Library and a Rocks FT_Memory. Three paths still use the standard allocator because FreeType does not pass FT_Memory to them: libpng in sfnt/pngshim.c (png_create_read_struct) and Brotli in sfnt/sfwoff2.c (BrotliDecoderDecompress).",
    "Not imported: bitmap font drivers (bdf, pcf, winfonts, pfr), PostScript outline formats (type1, cid, type42), the cache subsystem, the validators, the FreeType SDF renderer (msdfgen is used instead), the OT-SVG hooks and the Apple experimental hvf driver.",
    "RocksFtSystem.c (glue) replaces src/base/ftsystem.c, the FreeType system layer that FreeType documents as replaceable: no CRT file IO (FT_Stream_Open fails, faces come from memory or caller streams), and FT_New_Memory returns no memory object, so FT_Init_FreeType fails and every library is made with FT_New_Library and a Rocks FT_Memory."
  ],
  "modifications": [
    {
      "file": "include/freetype/config/ftoption.h",
      "upstreamSha256": "2115ceb051433d1596a63649923ace29441debd9f10de43c4c61259fc7b81384",
      "reason": "Build configuration (Docs/Design/Font/08-ThirdParty.ko.md section 8.2): turn off FT_CONFIG_OPTION_ENVIRONMENT_PROPERTIES (the FREETYPE_PROPERTIES environment variable would change rendering per machine), LZW, Mac resource-fork fonts and the OT-SVG hooks; turn on the system zlib (Core Zlib instead of the bundled copy), PNG (colour bitmap glyphs), Brotli (WOFF2), error strings and TT_CONFIG_OPTION_GPOS_KERNING (pair kerning from GPOS for FT_Get_Kerning, decision FD19)."
    },
    {
      "file": "include/freetype/config/ftmodule.h",
      "upstreamSha256": "f695657e4a8b02427296414d144d9dafc5b073538718d5e0c4290ba9d318c579",
      "reason": "Module list limited to the imported modules: autofit, truetype, cff, psaux, psnames, pshinter, sfnt, smooth and raster1 (the other drivers and renderers are not imported)."
    },
    {
      "file": "include/freetype/config/ftstdlib.h",
      "upstreamSha256": "de81744697b6f9f7fe3a49ca320f2a7ea8f2ae905bb96ff161b5b2d1eed25fe2",
      "reason": "ft_strcpy copies with ft_memcpy and ft_strlen instead of strcpy (same result for the non-overlapping strings FreeType copies in sfnt/sfdriver.c), because the Microsoft CRT marks strcpy deprecated and the engine warning rules reject it (-Wdeprecated-declarations). FreeType documents this header as the place to replace standard functions."
    }
  ],
  "patch": "Rocks.patch"
}
